WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.313
<v Captain>Beat to quarters! Every gun crew aboard follows the same drill,

2
00:00:06.313 --> 00:00:09.728
<v Captain>over and over. So does every processor.

3
00:00:10.378 --> 00:00:15.702
<v Alba>The processor and main memory, joined by three buses:

4
00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:20.975
<v Alba>the address bus, the data bus and the control bus.

5
00:00:21.625 --> 00:00:26.924
<v Alba>Step 1: the processor sets up the address bus with the address of the instruction.

6
00:00:27.124 --> 00:00:28.617
<v Captain>Locker 04!

7
00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:35.524
<v Alba>Step 2: the processor activates the read line on the control bus.

8
00:00:36.174 --> 00:00:45.449
<v Alba>Step 3: the instruction travels along the data bus into the instruction register,

9
00:00:45.449 --> 00:00:50.165
<v Alba>and the program counter steps on to 05.

10
00:00:50.815 --> 00:00:55.397
<v Alba>Step 4: the instruction is decoded and executed.

11
00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:56.373
<v Captain>Fire!

12
00:00:57.023 --> 00:01:01.995
<v Alba>To speed up the drill: more cores, more crews firing at once.

13
00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:12.783
<v Alba>A wider data bus: more bits per trip. More cache: fewer slow trips to main memory.

14
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:17.782
<v Alba>A higher clock speed: a faster drumbeat, more cycles per second.

15
00:01:18.432 --> 00:01:22.999
<v Captain>Address bus. Read line. Data bus. Decode and execute.

16
00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:26.093
<v Captain>Learn it like your drill, cadets.

